	      ABCL/R2 Gesi (the Summer Solstice) version
		    (version 0.50: June 21, 1993)
		  (version 0.60: Septempber 8, 1998)

This distribution kit contains an implementation of ABCL/R2 system
which is an object-oriented concurrent reflective language based on
Hybrid Group Architecture.  As a reflective language, an ABCL/R2
program can dynamically control its own behavior, such as scheduling
policy, from within user-program.  As an object-oriented concurrent
language, this system has almost all functions of ABCL/1.


Currently, we have tested the system on the following Common Lisp systems:
    o KCl (Kyoto Common Lisp)  Nov 13, 1990 (on SUN/SparcStations),
    o AKCL (Austin Kyoto Common Lisp)  Version(1.625)
      (on SUN/SparcStations),
    o CMU Common Lisp 17e (on SUN/SparcStations),
    o Macintosh Common Lisp 2.0,
    o Sun Common Lisp (on SUN/SparcStations),
    o Allegro CL 4.1, 4.2 [SPARC; R1] (on SUN/SparcStations)
             and 5.0.beta [Linux/X86], and
    o CLISP version February 1994 (on SUN/SparcStations)
(We have also tested on ACL\PC (Allegro Common Lisp for Windows)
version 1.0, and it has worked.  If you are interested in the ACL\PC
version, please contact us.)

To build the system, please read `install' file (and `readme-mcl' for
MCL users).

If you have any troubles, questions, suggestions or comments, please
feel free to contact the following address:

